# Case Study: Oracle Financial Cloud ERP — Overview

## Quick Facts
- **Client**: Regional healthcare network, 14 hospitals, 3,200 beds, $2.4B revenue
- **Engagement**: 32 weeks, $720K, 10-person team
- **Completion**: November 2025
- **Status**: Successfully completed

## Problem
6 acquisitions created 14 separate GL instances with no standardization. Manual consolidation required 8 FTEs for 15 days monthly. Inconsistent revenue recognition, no real-time visibility.

## Solution
Oracle Fusion Cloud Financials implementation:
- Unified chart of accounts (8 segments)
- GL, AP, AR, Cash Management modules
- Integration with Workday HRIS, patient billing, supply chain
- 340-user security role design
- Oracle Analytics Cloud for reporting

## Approach
- Big-bang for GL (single source of truth)
- Phased for AP (lower risk)
- 80% standardization, 20% local flexibility
- 47 stakeholder interviews, 6 consensus workshops
- 3 mock closes with parallel running

## Results
| Metric | Before | After |
|--------|--------|-------|
| Financial Close | 15 days | 4 days (-73%) |
| AP Processing | $12.50/invoice | $7.75/invoice (-38%) |
| Invoice Accuracy | 87% | 99.4% |
| GL Instances | 14 | 1 unified |

## Key Differentiators Demonstrated
- Oracle Platinum Partner specialization
- Healthcare regulatory expertise
- Change management (85 users trained)
- Data migration complexity (14 systems normalized)

## Technologies
Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP, Oracle Integration Cloud, Oracle Analytics Cloud, Oracle Identity Cloud

## Relevance
Primary reference for Oracle ERP implementations, especially healthcare and multi-entity consolidation. Demonstrates both technical capability and organizational change management.
